The audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the West Virginia Class E knowledge examination, reading at a plain-English level with no prior driving knowledge assumed. Section Ten teaches how to turn, back, park and follow safely and which parking places the law forbids. It depends on the signals and markings chapter for turn-on-red signals and center lines and on the definitions chapter for right-of-way and roadway. The rules progress from turning, through changing direction and backing, to parking rules, prohibited places, parking procedures and following distance.
